# winemac: Simplify Cocoa OpenGL context / views management.
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/11989 state=opened
# Very honestly I have no idea what this code was doing but it seems to me that it is unnecessary and as far as I can tell things are still working after removing it.

Client surfaces are updated when they are resized from win32u, the GL drawables latch their surface size whenever the surface is accessed and a opengl_drawable_flush is triggered. As far as I can tell this should always end up refreshing the macOS context, updating the backing size if necessary.
